/-!
# Exactly one root per system: `ν Antiprism.PentagonalAntiprism.polyhedron`

`prismPentagonalAntiprism_nu_system_<j>`: the systems of `prismPentagonalAntiprism_exact` (`Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismPentagonalAntiprism.Exact`), each with an interval added for each coordinate of its vertices in contact (the coordinate's integer part; the equations and the other intervals are unchanged). Each has
**exactly one real solution with every variable in its interval** (`prismPentagonalAntiprism_nu_system_<j>_oneRoot`:
`PolynomialSystem.HasUniqueRoot`, `Modules/System/PolyRootOf.lean`), and `ν Antiprism.PentagonalAntiprism.polyhedron` is the largest scale among
those roots (`prismPentagonalAntiprism_nu_roots_list`). `prismPentagonalAntiprism_nu_roots` is the statement in Mathlib's terms alone
(`IsPolyRootMax`, `Modules/System/PolyRoot.lean`), which implies that of the headline `prismPentagonalAntiprism_nu`
(`IsPolyRootMax.isPolynomialSystemMax`). A solution of a system gives a zero of its root's system in the box of Krawczyk's test, which is the only one (`Root.exists_scale`): that fixes the scale, the pose, the translation and the multipliers; the generator is the only root of its equation in its interval, and each coordinate is fixed by its equation (`Root.IsSystemOf.oneRoot`, `Modules/Root/HasUniqueRoot.lean`). The maximum is that of `prismPentagonalAntiprism_exact_list`: each completed system has the scales of its written-out system (`Root.IsSystemOf.scales_eq`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismPentagonalAntiprism` and `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismPentagonalAntiprism.Exact`,
which it does not change.
-/

